From: PS5_Proton <local@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] server: preserve advisory zero send buffers on PS5

PS5 native sockets reject SO_SNDBUF=0 with EINVAL. Windows applications can
request zero and expect it to remain readable while TCP still transfers data.
Reuse the existing Apple-host handling at the shared wineserver socket boundary.
A game launcher produces 67 rejected requests before its transport error; paired asset-free
probes compare option transitions and loopback traffic against pinned Linux Wine.

diff --git a/server/sock.c b/server/sock.c
--- a/server/sock.c
+++ b/server/sock.c
@@ -3429,10 +3429,10 @@
         }
         sndbuf = *(DWORD *)get_req_data();
 
-#ifdef __APPLE__
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__PROSPERO__)
         if (!sndbuf)
         {
-            /* setsockopt fails if a zero value is passed */
+            /* Native sockets reject zero; Windows keeps it as an advisory size. */
             sock->sndbuf = sndbuf;
             return;
         }
